Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: the name server telling the watchers of a mount prefix at the check-in of a mount there (netname_notify_mount()): a watcher that asked before the mount is never told.  mount_test's [33] watches /mount_test before it mounts it, and finds nothing on its port at the check-in.
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: mount_test: \[33\] WRONG — a watcher of "/": 0x0, its port; one of /mount_test: before the mount 0x10004003 \(nothing is 0x10004003\), mounted, at the check-in 0x10004003, not told its port; netname_wait_mount\("/"\): its port
Note: a watcher of a prefix already mounted is still told at once, which [33] asks first.

